  "summary": "GitPython before 3.1.59 contains an arbitrary file read vulnerability in TagReference.create() where a positional…",
  "details": "GitPython before 3.1.59 contains an arbitrary file read vulnerability in TagReference.create() where a positional reference parameter bypasses the unsafe option guard. Attackers can supply a reference value like --file=<path> to read arbitrary files, with contents returned in the annotated tag message.",
